## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a pragmatic CBA for on-device decision logic that changes user experience while preserving privacy and reducing server load. Tests modeling of energy, storage, and regulatory costs alongside rollout governance.

## Key Concepts

- On-device decisioning and privacy
- Compute and energy modeling
- Data minimization and consent logging
- Telemetry footprint and storage planning
- Rollout gates and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo cost model for CBA
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.cpuW * params.hours;
  const storage = params.rulesKB * params.devices / 1024;
  const savings = params.backendCostPerUnit * params.throughputReduction;
  const compliance = params.complianceCost;
  return energy + storage - savings + compliance;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate energy estimates across device SKUs?
- How would you adapt the model for regional regulatory differences?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about cost-benefit tradeoffs for on-device prefetching and privacy-friendly design in a beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- On-device caching and prefetching strategies
- Resource budgets: energy, memory, data
- Privacy and consent controls
- Observability: cache hit rate, latency, drift
- Rollout strategy and break-even planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight prefetch example (pseudo)
async function prefetchAssets(urls, cache) {
  for (const u of urls) {
    try {
      const resp = await fetch(u, {mode: 'no-cors', credentials: 'omit'});
      if (resp.ok) await cache.put(u, resp.clone());
    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure energy impact on mobile vs desktop?
- How would you ensure privacy compliance and opt-in UX for prefetching?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests candidate ability to design a mixed on-device/offload chat triage, evaluating lifecycle costs and business impact of privacy-preserving UX.

## Key Concepts

- On-device NLP model size and latency
- Cloud handoff economics
- Local storage and OTA updates
- Compliance and user trust
- Rollout and measurement plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for on-device classifier trigger
function triage(input) {
  const intent = onDeviceModel.predict(input);
  if (isComplex(intent)) {
    return cloudHandoff(input);
  }
  return generateResponse(intent);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure incremental savings from reduced cloud fetches?
- What telemetry would you collect to monitor quality without compromising privacy?

